`,e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["While the flag is enabled, every ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"helm upgrade"})," creates the ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"<chart fullname>-ca-to-kms-migration"})," Job (",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"lamassu-ca-to-kms-migration"})," for release ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"lamassu"}),"); a fresh install does not create it. Its hook weight is ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"-10"}),", so it runs before the other pre-upgrade hooks: the authorization bootstrap configuration (weight ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"-4"}),") and the database-migration Job (weight ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"-3"}),")."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["The Job consumes the same KMS service configuration the chart renders into the KMS ConfigMap, including the engines from ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"services.kms.cryptoEngines"}),", and runs the migration tool defined in ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"migrations.caToKms.image"}),". It mounts that configuration read-only at ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml"})," from the ConfigMap key ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"config"}),", so configure the destination engine in your values before the upgrade that performs the migration."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["The Job resolves its configuration through a projected volume with two optional sources: the release-scoped ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"<chart fullname>-kms-config"})," (",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"lamassu-kms-config"})," for release ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"lamassu"}),", ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"prod-lamassu-kms-config"})," for release ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"prod"}),") and the legacy unscoped ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"kms-config"})," created by chart versions before release-scoped naming. The legacy configuration remains authoritative while it is still present, and the release-scoped one is used once the legacy one is gone. Both sources are optional, so a missing ConfigMap never leaves the upgrade pod in ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"ContainerCreating"}),"."]}),`
